abstract: >-
  purgedcv implements purging and embargoing of overlapping labels,
  walk-forward validation, purged and group-purged k-fold, Combinatorial
  Purged Cross-Validation (CPCV) with backtest-path reconstruction, and the
  Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio, Deflated Sharpe Ratio, and Minimum Track
  Record Length. Every splitter follows the scikit-learn splitter protocol,
  the package is fully typed (passes mypy strict), and the implementation is
  pinned by an end-to-end test suite. The algorithms are due to Marcos Lopez
  de Prado (2018) and Bailey and Lopez de Prado (2012, 2014); this library
  is an open, MIT-licensed, sklearn-native implementation.
